Changelog: 09-11-2026 14:43:34

Release 6.2.0.

Changelog: 09-11-2026 13:59:20

Fixed. A game whose param.sfo gives its title (or another text) a shorter length than it has shows its whole
title in Your games: the text is read to its terminator within the entry's room, never into the next entry, as
Vita3K reads it since build 4282, which installs such games (4269 refused them).

Changelog: 09-11-2026 13:16:38

Added. The app installs Vita3K build 4282 (was 4269), the newest build: emulator.py pins build 4282 (0.2.1, commit
4b3addb3), the SHA-256 GitHub publishes for vita3k-4282-4b3addb3-windows-x86_64.7z (b97632bd…8dbc) and its size. The
archive holds the same 136 files by name, only Vita3K.exe changed; what the app relies on in Vita3K's source (the
command line, the portable folder, config.yml, the window settings with confirmExitApp, the firmware check, the game
and library windows) is unchanged. Vita3K's library window shows when a game has an update and filters its list.
The pin no longer follows the BC250 suite's, which stays on build 4269. The wiki says so.

