Release 4.1.0.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 00:23:01

Added. A warning when the device runs hot during a game (core's heat.py; owner, 02-11-2026): when the CPU or the GPU stays above 90 °C for half a minute, a banner shows at the top of the screen over Vita3K and the controller rumbles three times, again at most every five minutes; the game goes on. When the game ends, the log says how hot the chip got and for how long. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 23:28:28

Added. The shortcut of a game no longer in Vita3K's storage no longer starts Vita3K: it shows a screen that says the game is no longer there (core's gone screen; owner, 01-11-2026). The pane's information and the wiki say so.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 22:54:19

Added. LT Refresh on Your games reads the game folders again: a game or a package put there while the app is open shows at once, and the status line says when Steam no longer matches the marks. Before, the list was read only when the app started (owner, 01-11-2026). The pane's information and the wiki say so.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 21:51:44

Release 4.0.1.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 18:11:40

Release 4.0.0.

Changelog: 01-11-2026 16:39:16

Breaking. No folder or file is browsed to any more (owner, 30-10-2026: fixed folders, no folder selecting): LB
Firmware and RB Install a game on the Vita3K pane, with their browser (core's browse) and the folders it remembered,
are gone. The firmware files and the games are put in the app's own folders instead. LB on Your games is Steam artwork
now (it was RB), since RB on a game removes it.

Added. The app's own folders: Games\Vita in the user's folder, made with Games\Vita\Firmware when the app opens, and
Games\Vita on each SD card or USB drive that has one (library.fixed(), removable_drives(); an empty card slot is
none). The .PUP files put in Games\Vita\Firmware, or in a folder right below it (Sony names all three
PSP2UPDAT.PUP), are given to Vita3K by itself, the largest first, one after the other, when the app opens, when the
Vita3K card gets the focus and after Vita3K is installed (owner, 01-11-2026: firmware taken in automatically;
sync_firmware(), library.firmware_files()). Each file is given
once while it stays the same (its size and time kept in the app's settings), one Vita3K could not use too; a file
replaced is given again. The files stay. While the firmware is missing, the status line names the folder.

Added. The games put in the Games\Vita folders (and up to three folders below) that are not installed yet are short
rows of Your games, "VPK", "ZIP", "PKG" or "Folder" (a dumped game's folder; library.waiting(): the title and ID read
from its param.sfo, a .pkg's ID from its header; a game installed already is left out, an update and a .pkg not):
A installs one, X Install all installs every .vpk, .zip and folder one after the other, and A on a .pkg asks for its
license key on its page first (B goes back to its row). Nothing is deleted on its own (owner, 01-11-2026: before
deleting anything, let the user decide what to keep; core's keep.py): once the install ends, a page lists the .vpk,
.zip and .pkg files that brought something into Vita3K's storage, each with its size and marked Delete; A turns a
row to Keep and back, X deletes the rows still marked Delete, B goes back and deletes nothing. A file kept there is
not listed to install again until it changes (its size and time kept in the app's settings). A dumped folder is
never offered: it stays. The summary counts the games to install, and the Log
pane shows where Games\Vita is.

Added. RB Remove game on a game of Your games: a page lists what of the game would go, each on a row with its size
and marked Delete (owner, 01-11-2026: before deleting anything, let the user decide what to keep; core's keep.py):
the game in Vita3K's storage (ux0\app\<ID>), its update (ux0\patch) and extra content (ux0\addcont) when they are
there, and its shortcut in Steam when it is in Steam (library.removal(), removal_items()). A turns a row to Keep
and back; X deletes the rows still marked Delete, the shortcut through Steam, off the window's thread, read-only
files too, and the line says what was deleted and what was kept; B goes back and deletes nothing. The saves
(ux0\user\00\savedata) are never on the page. It does not work while Vita3K runs.

Fixed. The newest line of the Log pane stays in view when the rows above it take more room once laid out (the scroll
range grew after the box was scrolled to its end).

